BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 211.15 Tm (local database, validates the current record, and commits one complete transaction. UNIQUE constraints protect source) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 195.92 Tm (keys, event keys, and settlement references. Canonical payload comparison distinguishes a safe retry from a conflicting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 180.70 Tm (reuse of an identifier. A repeated request either returns its previous outcome or fails explicitly; it cannot silently post) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 165.47 Tm (twice. Workflow updates additionally compare the expected state and require exactly one affected row. Journal rows) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 150.25 Tm (express balanced double-entry amounts in a single immutable record, eliminating an intermediate half-posted journal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 135.02 Tm (WAL mode supports readers while SQLite serializes writers. Keep the database on a supported local filesystem, not a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 119.80 Tm (shared network mount. Multiple application hosts require a properly implemented transactional database service rather) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 104.57 Tm (than copied database files. These controls remove application-level check-then-write races for cooperating local) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 89.35 Tm (writers; they do not make external banking or servicer APIs exactly-once. No module sends payments. Import) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 74.12 Tm (independently confirmed settlements after external execution, preserving the provider's reference. A future payment) Tj ET
